experiment: halfcenter
  instrument        halfcenter   trial seed 0000000001357009   1200000 ticks
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)
  seed family       offset 288559 -> first creature 0000000001398ef8 (FRESH)
  shipped genome    adapt_jump 0.00, halfcenter_gain 0.00 (both OFF,
                    pinned hash ad96f882becbee92)
  normaliser        v75: inhibition / target_rate_hz = 5.00 Hz, which depends
                    on NEITHER half, so within-population coupling is 0 and
                    Baruzzi's condition holds. Between-coupling is g/T, TWICE
                    what v57 gave at the same nominal gain -- so g' = g/2
                    matches v57's coupling and g = 0.60 here is double it.
  what adaptclock   a fatigue current at the DERIVED constant produced no
  actually showed   clock: peak frequency followed tau_a with exponent +0.104
                    where a relaxation oscillator requires 1.000, and the peak
                    never left the 3.0-3.9 Hz band the pre-existing resonance
                    already occupies.
  what was WRONG    only ONE of two ingredients had been built. Matsuoka 1985:
  with it           mutual inhibition ALONE settles into a winner, ADAPTATION
                    is what makes it oscillate. Both, wired as two mutually
                    inhibiting populations. v32's kernel is local-minus-field-
                    mean -- a bump kernel, not two populations taking turns.
                    So v56 is a PREREQUISITE, not a failed attempt.

  THE 2x2, AND THE THEORY MAKES TWO NULL PREDICTIONS
    neither   -/-   nothing
    fatigue   +/-   nothing (and adaptclock already measured exactly that)
    inhibNN   -/+   SETTLES into a winner, no rhythm
    bothNN    +/+   OSCILLATES
  Two pre-registered nulls are two chances for the theory to be wrong in a
  way a single contrast against the double-off baseline could not see.

  PRE-REGISTERED
    PRIMARY, an INTERACTION: a `both` arm's anti-phase correlation must beat
      BOTH its own singles, not merely `neither`.
    THE SIGNATURE     corr(lower-half rate, upper-half rate) must go NEGATIVE.
                      A half-center ALTERNATES; a resonance moves both halves
                      TOGETHER. This is the mechanism itself rather than a
                      spectral proxy -- no frequency grid, no argmax, and the
                      pre-existing 3 Hz ring cannot produce it. Bar: <= -0.20
                      and >= 3 SE below each single.
    frequency         within the `both` tau arms, report the EXPONENT on
                      log(peak f) vs log(1/tau) -- adaptclock's lesson: a
                      correlation passed 0.80 there while the slope was ten
                      times too shallow. Required ~1.0.
    KILL SWITCH       duty bounded AWAY FROM BOTH ENDS and rate near target.
                      v32's first lateral form ran vocal at 66 Hz against 4.4
                      with duty pinned at 1.00, and a runaway looks like a
                      strong result on any ratio statistic.
    BOTH HALVES       anti-phase reported per half of the recording, because
                      the self_gain sweep died exactly there.
    argmax null       peak SNR vs `neither`'s PEAK over the same 24 bins.
                      adaptclock measured that null at ~3.9, never 1.0.
    refusal           anti-phase stays >= 0 in every `both` arm -> reciprocal
                      inhibition plus fatigue does not alternate HERE even
                      though the textbook says it must, which would point at
                      the rate code itself rather than at any missing part.

